<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                   xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
        Activate the externally managed users that the student import left unactivated.

        UserCreationService.createUser used to set activated = false and generate an activation key for every user it created,
        external (LDAP/SAML) ones included. Course import, exam registration and admin user import all resolve unknown students
        through UserService.findUserInLdap, which uses that factory and never activated the result - unlike the LDAP first-login
        path, which activated the user immediately afterwards. Whether an external user ended up activated therefore depended on
        nothing more than whether they logged in before an instructor imported them.

        This stayed invisible because LdapAuthenticationProvider is the only authentication provider that does not check
        `activated`. Once git authentication started enforcing account state, these users kept their web access but lost access to
        their repositories over both HTTPS and SSH.

        An activation key is only redeemable through GET /activate, which - like the mail that carries the key - is gated behind
        artemis.user-management.registration.enabled, and self-registration always creates internal users. For an external user the
        key is therefore unreachable state, which also makes it a reliable marker of an account created by this bug:

          - createUser set activated = false AND an activation key
          - deactivateUser sets activated = false and never sets a key

        Restricting the update to rows that still carry an activation key consequently repairs the import-created accounts while
        leaving deliberate administrative deactivations untouched. Internal users are excluded as well: an unactivated internal
        account with a key is a genuine abandoned self-registration and must stay unactivated.
    -->
    <changeSet id="20260820091251-01-activate-imported-external-users" author="krusche">
        <update tableName="jhi_user">
            <column name="activated" valueBoolean="true"/>
            <column name="activation_key" valueComputed="NULL"/>
            <where>activated = false AND is_internal = false AND is_deleted = false AND activation_key IS NOT NULL</where>
        </update>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
